            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0361" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114A/6–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-28">June 28,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received June 28—10:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3348. Am[erican] Interests—Japan. Your 1111, Mar 17. FonOff note June 26 states
                    during interview June 16 between Gorgé and Suzuki, latter declared Japan has not
                    undertaken obligation to bury POWs in all cases and all places.</p>
                <p>Suzuki stated moreover impossible carry out burials in large centers where Jap
                    themselves cremated. However at other places for example in the country, he
                    added, Jap authorities would assure burial of dead.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
